<title>USA: Sony cuts US price of PlayStation to $149.</title>
<headline>Sony cuts US price of PlayStation to $149.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp on Monday said it cut the price of its PlayStation video game console in the United States by $50 to $149 and the price of video game titles to $49.95.</p>
<p>With the cut, the PlayStation is priced $50 less than the Nintendo Co Ltd's Nintendo 64 console.</p>
<p>The move is expected to set off a price war in the video game hardware business and boost sales of video game software, analysts said.</p>
</text>
